{
  "title": "50: Qaf ق",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nقٓۚ وَالْقُرْاٰنِ الْمَجِيْدِۚ‏(1)\nQAAAF, WAL QUR-AANIL MAJEED.\nQaf. By the glorious Quran.\nبَلْ عَجِبُوْۤا اَنْ جَآءَهُمْ مُّنْذِرٌ مِّنْهُمْ فَقَالَ الْكٰفِرُوْنَ هٰذَا شَىْءٌ عَجِيْبٌ‌ۚ‏(2)\nBAL A’JEBOO AN JAAA-AHUM MUNZERUM MINHUM FA-QAALAL KAAFEROONA HAAZAA SHAY-UN A’JEEB.\nIndeed they consider it odd that a warner from among themselves should have come to them. So the faithless say, ‘This is an odd thing.’\nءَاِذَا مِتْنَا وَكُنَّا تُرَابًا ‌ۚ ذٰ لِكَ رَجْعٌ ۢ بَعِيْدٌ‏(3)\nA-EZAA MITNAA WA KUNNAA TORAABAA, ZAALEKA RAJ-U’M BA-E’ED.\n‘What! When we are dead and have become dust, [shall we be raised again]? That is a far-fetched return!’\nقَدْ عَلِمْنَا مَا تَنْقُصُ الْاَرْضُ مِنْهُمْ‌ۚ وَعِنْدَنَا كِتٰبٌ حَفِيْظٌ‏(4)\nQAD A’LIMNAA MAA TANQOSUL ARZO MINHUM, WA I’NDANAA KETAABUN HAFEEZ.\nWe know what the earth diminishes from them, and with Us is a preserving Book.\nبَلْ كَذَّبُوْا بِالْحَقِّ لَمَّا جَآءَهُمْ فَهُمْ فِىْۤ اَمْرٍ مَّرِيْجٍ‏(5)\nBAL KAZZABOO BIL-HAQQE LAMMAA JAAA-AHUM FAHUM FEE AMRIM MAREEJ.\nIndeed, they denied the truth when it came to them; so they are now in a perplexed state of affairs.\nاَ فَلَمْ يَنْظُرُوْۤا اِلَى السَّمَآءِ فَوْقَهُمْ كَيْفَ بَنَيْنٰهَا وَزَ يَّنّٰهَا وَمَا لَهَا مِنْ فُرُوْجٍ‏(6)\nAFALAM YANZOROO ELAS SAMAAA-E FAWQAHUM KAYFA BANAYNAAHAA WA ZAYYANNAAHAA WA MAA LAHAA MIN FOROOJ.\nHave they not, then, observed the heaven above them, how We have built it and adorned it, and that there are no cracks in it?\nوَالْاَرْضَ مَدَدْنٰهَا وَاَ لْقَيْنَا فِيْهَا رَوَاسِىَ وَاَنْۢبَتْنَا فِيْهَا مِنْ كُلِّ زَوْجٍۢ بَهِيْجٍ ۙ‏(7)\nWAL ARZA MADADNAAHAA WA ALQAYNAA FEEHAA RAWAASEYA WA AMBATNAA FEEHAA MIN KULLE ZAWJIM BAHEEJ.\nAnd We spread out the earth, and cast in it firm mountains, and caused every delightful kind [of vegetation] to grow in it.\nتَبْصِرَةً وَّذِكْرٰى لِكُلِّ عَبْدٍ مُّنِيْبٍ‏(8)\nTABSERATANW WA ZIKRAA LE-KULLE A’BDIM MONEEB.\n[In this there is] an insight and admonition for every penitent servant.\nوَنَزَّلْنَا مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءً مُّبٰرَكًا فَاَنْۢبَتْنَا بِهٖ جَنّٰتٍ وَّحَبَّ الْحَصِيْدِ ۙ‏(9)\nWA NAZZALNAA MENAS SAMAAA-E MAAA-AM MOBAARAKAN FA-AMBATNAA BEHI JANNAATINW WA HABBAL HASEED.\nWe send down from the sky salubrious water, with which We grow gardens and the grain which is harvested,\nوَالنَّخْلَ بٰسِقٰتٍ لَّهَا طَلْعٌ نَّضِيْدٌ ۙ‏(10)\nWAN NAKHLA BAASEQAATIL LAHAA TAL-U’N NAZEED.\nand tall date palms with regularly set spathes,\nرِّزْقًا لِّلْعِبَادِ‌ ۙ وَاَحْيَيْنَا بِهٖ بَلْدَةً مَّيْتًا‌ ؕ كَذٰلِكَ الْخُرُوْجُ‏(11)\nRIZQAL LIL-E’BAADE, WA AHYAYNAA BEHI BALDATAM MAYTAA, KAZAALEKAL KHOROOJ.\nas a provision for Our servants, and with it We revive a dead country. Likewise will be the rising [from the dead].\nكَذَّبَتْ قَبْلَهُمْ قَوْمُ نُوْحٍ وَّاَصْحٰبُ الرَّسِّ وَثَمُوْدُۙ‏(12)\nKAZZABAT QABLAHUM QAWMO NOOHINW WA ASHAABUR RASSE WA SAMOOD.\nThe people of Noah denied before them, and [so did] the people of Rass and Thamud,\nوَعَادٌ وَّفِرْعَوْنُ وَاِخْوَانُ لُوْطٍۙ‏(13)\nWA A’ADUNW WA FIR-A’WNO WA IKHWAANO LOOT.\nand ‘Ad, Pharaoh, and the brethren of Lot,\nوَّاَصْحٰبُ الْاَيْكَةِ وَقَوْمُ تُبَّعٍ‌ؕ كُلٌّ كَذَّبَ الرُّسُلَ فَحَقَّ وَعِيْدِ‏(14)\nWA ASHAABUL AYKATE WA QAWMO TUBBA’, KULLUN KAZZABAR ROSOLA FA-HAQQA WA-E’ED.\nand the inhabitants of Aykah and the people of Tubbac. Each [of them] impugned the apostles, and so My threat became due [against them].\nاَفَعَيِيْنَا بِالْخَلْقِ الْاَوَّلِ‌ؕ بَلْ هُمْ فِىْ لَبْسٍ مِّنْ خَلْقٍ جَدِيْدٍ‏(15)\nAFA-A’YEENAA BIL-KHALQIL AWWAL, BAL HUM FEE LABSIM MIN KHALQIN JADEED.\nHave We been exhausted by the first creation? No, they are in doubt about a new creation.\nوَلَقَدْ خَلَقْنَا الْاِنْسَانَ وَنَعْلَمُ مَا تُوَسْوِسُ بِهٖ نَفْسُهٗ ۖۚ وَنَحْنُ اَقْرَبُ اِلَيْهِ مِنْ حَبْلِ الْوَرِيْدِ‏(16)\nWA LAQAD KHALAQNAL INSAANA WA NA’LAMO MAA TOWASWESO BEHI NAFSOH, WA NAHNO AQRABO ELAYHE MIN HABLIL WAREED.\nCertainly We have created man and We know to what his soul tempts him, and We are nearer to him than his jugular vein.\nاِذْ يَتَلَقَّى الْمُتَلَقِّيٰنِ عَنِ الْيَمِيْنِ وَعَنِ الشِّمَالِ قَعِيْدٌ‏(17)\nIZ YATALAQQAL MOTALAQQEYAANE A’NIL YAMEENE WA A’NISH SHEMAALE QA-E’ED.\nWhen the twin recorders record [his deeds], seated on the right hand and on the left:\nمَا يَلْفِظُ مِنْ قَوْلٍ اِلَّا لَدَيْهِ رَقِيْبٌ عَتِيْدٌ‏(18)\nMAA YALFEZO MIN QAWLIN ILLAA LADAYHE RAQEEBUN A’TEED.\nhe says no word but that there is a ready observer beside him.\nوَ جَآءَتْ سَكْرَةُ الْمَوْتِ بِالْحَقِّ‌ؕ ذٰلِكَ مَا كُنْتَ مِنْهُ تَحِيْدُ‏(19)\nWA JAAA-AT SAKRATUL MAWTE BIL-HAQ, ZAALEKA MAA KUNTA MINHO TAHEED.\nThe throes of death bring the truth: ‘This is what you used to shun!’\nوَنُفِخَ فِى الصُّوْرِ ‌ؕ ذٰ لِكَ يَوْمُ الْوَعِيْدِ‏(20)\nWA NOFEKHA FIS SOOR, ZAALEKA YAWMUL WA-E’ED.\nAnd the Trumpet will be blown: ‘This is the promised day.’\nوَجَآءَتْ كُلُّ نَفْسٍ مَّعَهَا سَآئِقٌ وَّشَهِيْدٌ‏(21)\nWA JAAA-AT KULLO NAFSIM MA-A’HAA SAAA-EQUNW WA SHAHEED.\nEvery soul will come accompanied by [two angels], a driver, and a witness:\nلَقَدْ كُنْتَ فِىْ غَفْلَةٍ مِّنْ هٰذَا فَكَشَفْنَا عَنْكَ غِطَآءَكَ فَبَصَرُكَ الْيَوْمَ حَدِيْدٌ‏(22)\nLAQAD KUNTA FEE GHAFLATIM MIN HAAZAA FA-KASHAFNAA A’NKA GHETAAA-AKA FA-BASAROKAL YAWMA HADEED.\n[he will be told] ‘You were certainly oblivious of this. We have removed your veil from you, and so today your eyesight is acute.’\nوَقَالَ قَرِيْنُهٗ هٰذَا مَا لَدَىَّ عَتِيْدٌ ؕ‏(23)\nWA QAALA QAREENOHU HAAZAA MAA LADAYYA A’TEED.\nThen his companion [angel] will say, ‘This is what is ready with me [of his record of deeds].’\nاَلْقِيَا فِىْ جَهَنَّمَ كُلَّ كَفَّارٍ عَنِيْدٍۙ‏(24)\nALQEYAA FEE JAHANNAMA KULLA KAFFAARIN A’NEED.\n[The two angels accompany him will be told,] ‘Cast every obdurate ingrate into hell,\nمَّنَّاعٍ لِّلْخَيْرِ مُعْتَدٍ مُّرِيْبِ ۙ‏(25)\nMANNAA-I’L LIL-KHAYRE MO’TADIM MOREEB.\n[every] hinderer of good, transgressor, and skeptic,\nاۨلَّذِىْ جَعَلَ مَعَ اللّٰهِ اِلٰهًا اٰخَرَ فَاَ لْقِيٰهُ فِى الْعَذَابِ الشَّدِيْدِ‏(26)\nLAZEE JA-A’LA MA-A’L LAAHE ELAAHAN AAKHARA FA-ALQEYAAHO FIL A’ZAABISH SHADEED.\nwho had set up another god along with Allah and cast him into the severe punishment.’\nقَالَ قَرِيْنُهٗ رَبَّنَا مَاۤ اَطْغَيْتُهٗ وَلٰكِنْ كَانَ فِىْ ضَلٰلٍۢ بَعِيْدٍ‏(27)\nQAALA QAREENOHU RABBANAA MAA ATGHAYTOHU WA LAAKIN KAANA FEE ZALAALIM BA-E’ED.\nHis companion [devil] will say, ‘Our Lord! I did not incite him to rebel [against You], but he was [himself] in extreme error.’\nقَالَ لَا تَخْتَصِمُوْا لَدَىَّ وَقَدْ قَدَّمْتُ اِلَيْكُمْ بِالْوَعِيْدِ‏(28)\nQAALA LAA TAKHTASEMOO LADAYYA WA QAD QADDAMTO ELAYKUM BIL-WA-E’ED.\nHe will say, ‘Do not wrangle in My presence, for I had already warned you in advance.\nمَا يُبَدَّلُ الْقَوْلُ لَدَىَّ وَمَاۤ اَنَا بِظَلَّامٍ لِّلْعَبِيْدِ‏(29)\nMAA YOBADDALUL QAWLO LADAYYA WA MAA ANAA BE-ZALLAAMIL LIL-A’BEED.\nThe word [of judgement] is unalterable with Me, and I am not tyrannical to My servants.’\nيَوْمَ نَقُوْلُ لِجَهَنَّمَ هَلِ امْتَلَئْتِ وَتَقُوْلُ هَلْ مِنْ مَّزِيْدٍ‏(30)\nYAWMA NAQOOLO LE-JAHANNAMA HALIM TALAATE WA TAQOOLO HAL MIM MAZEED.\nThe day when We shall say to hell, ‘Are you full?’ It will say, ‘Is there any more?’\nوَاُزْلِفَتِ الْجَنَّةُ لِلْمُتَّقِيْنَ غَيْرَ بَعِيْدٍ‏(31)\nWA UZLEFATIL JANNATO LIL-MUTTAQEENA GHAYRA BA-E’ED.\nAnd paradise will be brought near for the Godwary, it will not be distant [any more]:\nهٰذَا مَا تُوْعَدُوْنَ لِكُلِّ اَوَّابٍ حَفِيْظٍ‌ۚ‏(32)\nHAAZAA MAA TOO-A’DOONA LE-KULLE AWWAABIN HAFEEZ.\n‘This is what you were promised. [It is] for every penitent and dutiful [servant]\nمَنْ خَشِىَ الرَّحْمٰنَ بِالْغَيْبِ وَجَآءَ بِقَلْبٍ مُّنِيْبِۙ‏(33)\nMAN KHASHEYAR RAHMAANA BIL-GHAYBE WA JAAA-A BE-QALBIM MONEEB.\nwho fears the All-beneficent in secret and comes with a penitent heart.\nاۨدْخُلُوْهَا بِسَلٰمٍ‌ؕ ذٰلِكَ يَوْمُ الْخُلُوْدِ‏(34)\nUDKHOLOOHAA BE-SALAAM, ZAALEKA YAWMUL KHOLOOD.\nEnter it in peace! This is the day of immortality.’\nلَهُمْ مَّا يَشَآءُوْنَ فِيْهَا وَلَدَيْنَا مَزِيْدٌ‏(35)\nLAHUM MAA YASHAAA-OONA FEEHAA WA LADAYNAA MAZEED.\nThere they will have whatever they wish, and with Us there is yet more.\nوَكَمْ اَهْلَكْنَا قَبْلَهُمْ مِّنْ قَرْنٍ هُمْ اَشَدُّ مِنْهُمْ بَطْشًا فَنَقَّبُوْا فِى الْبِلَادِ ؕ هَلْ مِنْ مَّحِيْصٍ‏(36)\nWA KAM AHLAKNAA QABLAHUM MIN QARNIN HUM ASHADDO MINHUM BATSHAN FA-NAQQABOO FIL BELAAD, HAL MIM MAHEES.\nHow many generations We have destroyed before them, who were stronger than these, insomuch that they ransacked the towns?! So, is there any escape [from Allah’s punishment]?\nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰلِكَ لَذِكْرٰى لِمَنْ كَانَ لَهٗ قَلْبٌ اَوْ اَلْقَى السَّمْعَ وَهُوَ شَهِيْدٌ‏(37)\nINNA FEE ZAALEKA LA-ZIKRAA LEMAN KAANA LAHU QALBUN AW ALQAS SAM-A’ WA HOWA SHAHEED.\nThere is indeed an admonition in that for one who has a heart, or gives ear, being attentive.\nوَلَقَدْ خَلَقْنَا السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا فِىْ سِتَّةِ اَيَّامٍ‌ۖ وَّمَا مَسَّنَا مِنْ لُّغُوْبٍ‏(38)\nWA LAQAD KHALAQNAS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA WA MAA BAYNAHOMAA FEE SITTATE AYYAAM, WA MAA MASSANAA MIL LOGHOOB.\nCertainly We created the heavens and the earth, and whatever is between them, in six days, and any fatigue did not touch Us.\nفَاصْبِرْ عَلٰى مَا يَقُوْلُوْنَ وَسَبِّحْ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّكَ قَبْلَ طُلُوْعِ الشَّمْسِ وَقَبْلَ الْغُرُوْبِ‌ۚ‏(39)\nFASBIR A’LAA MAA YAQOOLOONA WA SABBEH BE-HAMDE RABBEKA QABLA TOLOO-I’SH SHAMSE WA QABLAL GHOROOB.\nSo be patient at what they say, and celebrate the praise of your Lord before the rising of the sun and before the sunset,\nوَمِنَ الَّيْلِ فَسَبِّحْهُ وَاَدْبَارَ السُّجُوْدِ‏(40)\nWA MENAL LAYLE FA-SABBEHHO WA ADBAARAS SOJOOD.\nand glorify Him through part of the night and after the prostrations.\nوَاسْتَمِعْ يَوْمَ يُنَادِ الْمُنَادِ مِنْ مَّكَانٍ قَرِيْبٍۙ‏(41)\nWAS TAME’ YAWMA YONAADIL MONAADE MIM MAKAANIN QAREEB.\nAnd be on the alert for the day when the caller calls from a close quarter,\nيَوْمَ يَسْمَعُوْنَ الصَّيْحَةَ بِالْحَقِّ‌ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ يَوْمُ الْخُرُوْجِ‏(42)\nYAWMA YASMA-O’ONAS SAYHATA BIL-HAQ, ZAALEKA YAWMUL KHOROOJ.\nthe day when they hear the Cry in all truth. That is the day of rising [from the dead].\nاِنَّا نَحْنُ نُحْىٖ وَنُمِيْتُ وَاِلَيْنَا الْمَصِيْرُۙ‏(43)\nINNAA NAHNO NOHYEE WA NOMEETO WA ELAYNAL MASEER.\nIndeed it is We who give life and bring death, and toward Us is the [final] destination.\nيَوْمَ تَشَقَّقُ الْاَرْضُ عَنْهُمْ سِرَاعًا‌ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ حَشْرٌ عَلَيْنَا يَسِيْرٌ‏(44)\nYAWMA TASHAQQAQUL ARZO A’NHUM SERAA-A’A, ZAALEKA HASHRUN A’LAYNAA YASEER.\nThe day the earth is split open for [disentombing] them, [they will come out] hastening. That mustering is easy for Us [to carry out].\nنَحْنُ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا يَقُوْلُوْنَ‌ وَمَاۤ اَنْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ بِجَبَّارٍ‌ فَذَكِّرْ بِالْقُرْاٰنِ مَنْ يَّخَافُ وَعِيْدِ‏(45)\nNAHNO A-A’LAMO BEMAA YAQOOLOONA WA MAA ANTA A’LAYHIM BE-JABBAAR, FA-ZAKKIR BIL-QUR-AANE MAN-Y YAKHAAFO WA-E’ED.\nWe know well what they say, and you are not there to compel them. So admonish by the Quran those who fear My threat.",
  "merits": "Surah Qaaf\nThis Surah is ‘Makki’ and it has 45 verses. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that whoever recites this Surah frequently will not suffer at the time of death. Reciting Surah Qaaf in salaat increases one’s sustenance and makes the accounting of the Day of Judgement easy.\nWriting and drinking water in which this Surah has been dissolved cures one of many acute diseases. Verse 23 of this Surah is especially good for the cure of eye ailments. One can recite this verse and blow into some water and then drink it, and by the will of Allah (s.w.t.) any problem with eyes will be cured."
}
